 "guarantees": [
  {
   "id": "views.stable",
   "text": "A view, column or type in `views` is not renamed, removed or retyped without a compatibility view and a CHANGELOG.md entry first. New views and columns may appear at any time."
  },
  {
   "id": "current_row.order",
   "text": "`<table>` returns, per key in `keys`, the `<table>_log` row that `ORDER BY scraped_at DESC, <each column of tie_order> ASC NULLS LAST` puts first. A table rebuilt whole returns its current build; an append-only table every row."
  },
  {
   "id": "arrow.end_of_stream",
   "text": "A complete `format: arrow` answer of POST /v1/sql ends with the Arrow IPC end-of-stream marker (FF FF FF FF 00 00 00 00), also with no rows. An answer cut by a failure or the query deadline ends the connection without it: a body without the marker is a cut answer."
  },
  {
   "id": "write_times.gate",
   "text": "GET /v1/health `write_times.tables[<table>].ok` is false while a Parquet file of the table modified after its write-time start M holds rows without `scraped_at`, or while the table needs an M and has none; `status` is then \"degraded\". A consumer that reads `<table>` or `<table>_at(T)` refuses to run while that entry is false; a table with no entry needs no M."
  },
  {
   "id": "freeze.reads",
   "text": "While `freeze.reads.active` is true, POST /v1/sql, GET /v1/tables, GET /v1/tables/{table}, POST /v1/ask and /mcp answer a client that is not allowed HTTP 423 with the reason. GET /v1/health (no token, no query slot) and GET /v1/status report the state (`schemas.freeze_state`). The write freeze does not stop reads. A consumer refuses to read while reads are frozen and it is not allowed, and treats an answer without these fields as a refusal."
  },
  {
   "id": "pin.at",
   "text": "`SELECT ... FROM <table>_at(T)` (T a TIMESTAMPTZ, a literal or a parameter) returns the table as it stood at lake time T, and the same rows on every later read: for a deduplicated table the current-row order over the `<table>_log` rows written at or before T (`scraped_at <= T`); for a table rebuilt whole the newest build written at or before T; for an append-only table the rows written at or before T. The bound is inclusive for every kind: a row or build written at exactly T is part of the table at T. It raises an error naming the table, instead of returning a result, when T is before the oldest build kept, when the build current at T is no longer kept, or when T is before the time an append-only table's rows got a write time. Builds are kept 30 days and at most 10 per table, and longer while a pin names them. `<table>` and `<table>_log` keep their meaning."
  }
 ]
